Two implementation choices worth noting:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- **Byte-at-a-time reading with a one-byte pushback slot**, rather than slurping stdin. [38;5;10mscanf[0m must read one character past the digit run to know where the number ends, and it consumes nothing more. Slurping would have changed blocking behavior; I verified both binaries emit [38;5;10m2a000000[0m and exit immediately given [38;5;10m42 [0m on a pipe held open for 5 seconds.[0m[0m
- **[38;5;10mto_ne_bytes[0m** for the byte dump, matching the host byte order that the C's [38;5;10m(unsigned char *)&x[0m cast observes (little-endian here).[0m[0m
